  "retained_change": "Strict interior sampling refines both algebraic owners and preserves progress on either side when the other next proof is unavailable. Root ordering, interval refinement, gap selection, and rational reconstruction share one retained Sturm bisection state. Exact midpoint arithmetic calls Hyperreal average_pair directly.",
  "exactness": {
    "reproduced_failure": "On 545d5b6, algebraic roots 3/4 and 7/8 with original isolators [1/2,1] returned 5/8 as their strict interior sample. The regression failed before the change and passes afterward.",
    "completeness": "An original lower bound of the right isolator need not lie above the left root. A one-sided search could therefore return an exterior point upon reaching an exact midpoint, or refine indefinitely for an irrational root. Both live owners now advance until their enclosing intervals prove a strict gap.",
    "certificates": "Non-root endpoint ownership, checked Sturm variation differences, exact midpoint witnesses, denominator bounds, continued-fraction reconstruction, and exact polynomial replay remain authoritative. Uncertain refinement preserves its previous enclosure, and an independently certified midpoint root is retained even if auxiliary Sturm evidence is unavailable.",
    "regressions": "Two new tests cover 48 rational, irrational, repeated-root, close-root, and mixed exact/algebraic combinations across both policies; irrational fixtures include positive rational, negative rational, and pi coefficient scaling. The existing 24-case reconstruction matrix also passes through the shared state.",
    "public_api_added": false,
    "compatibility_shims_added": false,
    "removed_interfaces": [
      "midpoint_real"
    ],
    "uncertainty_cache": "Only successful certificates are retained; unavailable evidence remains retryable."
